<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarai was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu Khan</a> in the 1240s near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan">Astrakhan</a>; a second capital, New Sarai, was built further upstream in the 14th century. Rus' princes travelled there to receive their patents to rule, and it grew into a large trading city with mosques, workshops and merchants' quarters. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> sacked it in 1395, and the Crimean khan destroyed what remained in 1502.</p></div>
